    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "GVM Auctioneers are delighted to introduce to the market this stunningly attractive split-level bungalow residence, superbly positioned on an impressive site extending to circa 1.2 statute acres. The property enjoys an elevated setting with spectacular panoramic views over the surrounding countryside, including views of three historic castles.\n\nThis impressive home is ideally located within walking distance of the picturesque and historic village of Bunratty, offering a wonderful combination of space, privacy, mature grounds and convenience.\n\nThe residence is thoughtfully laid out and provides generously proportioned accommodation comprising four good-sized bedrooms, three reception rooms, a kitchen, utility room and two bathrooms. The versatile layout offers excellent flexibility for modern family living and will particularly appeal to those seeking a substantial home in an enviable countryside setting. At lower-ground-floor level, the property also benefits from a garage and service room, providing valuable additional storage and utility space.\n\nExternally, the mature and beautifully established site is a particularly attractive feature of the property. The grounds are well sheltered and lined with mature trees, creating a high degree of privacy and a wonderful sense of seclusion. The entrance is especially appealing, with a distinctive sweeping driveway and a historic lime kiln positioned on the northern side of the site.\n\nThe location is exceptional, offering the tranquillity of a mature countryside setting while remaining within easy reach of major transport links and regional centres. Shannon Airport, Limerick City and Ennis are all readily accessible, while the property is conveniently positioned just off the dual carriageway network linking Limerick and Galway with the wider region.\n\nBunratty is renowned worldwide for its rich historical heritage, most notably Bunratty Castle and Folk Park, together with its excellent selection of visitor attractions, restaurants, traditional pubs and local amenities enjoyed by residents and visitors alike.\n\nProperties of this nature, combining a substantial mature site, magnificent views, generous accommodation and such a convenient location, rarely come to the market.\n\nInspection of this superb home is very highly recommended. The property is certain to impress prospective purchasers seeking a unique and highly desirable family home in a truly wonderful setting.\n\n Viewing is strictly by appointment with GVM Auctioneers."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance hallway - 4.06m (13'4\") x 2m (6'7\")\nBright and inviting\n\nLounge - 6.01m (19'9\") x 4.03m (13'3\")\nDual aspect with wonderful countryside views. Feature fireplace\n\nDining room - 3.07m (10'1\") x 3.02m (9'11\")\nSolid wood flooring\n\nKitchen - 5.04m (16'6\") x 3.07m (10'1\")\nFitted with generous floor and eye level presses.\nWalk in hotpress\n\nRear hallway with wc & whb off - 4.09m (13'5\") x 2m (6'7\")\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.04m (10'0\") x 3.02m (9'11\")\nDouble\n\nBedroom 2 - 4.04m (13'3\") x 3.04m (10'0\")\nMaser with built in wardrobes.\nEn suite off with shower\n\nBedroom 3 - 4m (13'1\") x 3m (9'10\")\nDouble with built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 4 - 4m (13'1\") x 3m (9'10\")\nDouble with built in wardrobes\n\nFull fitted main bathroom - 2.04m (6'8\") x 2.04m (6'8\")\n\nBasement\n\nGarage - 6m (19'8\") x 3.07m (10'1\")\n\nStore/Services room - 3.07m (10'1\") x 3.07m (10'1\")\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
